<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sappi says Adamas mill strike unresolved.</title>
<headline>Sappi says Adamas mill strike unresolved.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African paper company Sappi Ltd said on Monday that at a strike at its Adamas mill in Port Elizabeth which started on April 23 remained unresolved, but customers were continuing to receive supplies.</p>
<p>Some 200 workers, members of the Paper, Printing, Wood and Allied Workers' Union, are striking to demand a 10 percent annual wage increase. Sappi is offering an increase of six percent now with a further four percent in six months' time.</p>
<p>&quot;The situation at the mill remains quiet with no incidents reported. The mill's two paper machines are running and customers' supplies have been unaffected,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
